  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Existing execution, separate review",
      "items": [
        "Authorized preflight uses the existing lease/serial gate. Deterministic receipt bytes rely on cooperating wrapper use, not hostile-caller chronology.",
        "Recommendation launches no trial. Development must be unscoped; held-out primary/counterpart input content cannot reuse development inputs."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Limited same-host claim",
      "items": [
        "Selected trusted-maintainer receipts support not-supplied-to-author during the fixed comparison, not hostile same-UID secrecy. Unknown reads stay unknown.",
        "Remote anchor uncertainty is inconclusive, preserving independent development rejection. Local tampering rejects; known prior or during-comparison exposure blocks.",
        "Recheck held-out records after remote refresh and source after assessment. Two source checks share 12 seconds of Git/read time, excluding remote waits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Conformance is not actual benefit",
      "items": [
        "Positive CLI conformance uses FAKE lifecycle, qualification, clock, tool and remote-anchor evidence. No actual held-out comparison is claimed.",
        "A real reject or inconclusive is a valid endpoint. Source acceptance, merge and account installation require separate authority."
      ]
    }
  ]
